    {
      "finding": "Direct dependencies use exact --extern paths; maybe_load_library_crate returns command-line selection before directory search. Version/target/hash checks remain enabled. Transitive dependencies ignore direct --extern overrides and require discovery of the matching dependency hash, hence the narrow -L dependency directory containing the own literal escaper.",
      "source": "compiler/rustc_metadata/src/locator.rs:324"
    },
    {
      "finding": "ProcMacro prefers static linkage of Rust dependencies; the candidate client and its real literal dependency can be embedded in the macro dylib.",
      "source": "compiler/rustc_metadata/src/dependency_format.rs:121"
    },
    {
      "finding": "Loading a proc-macro crate returns an empty Rust dependency-number map. The caller loads the real macro dylib and its declaration symbol; it does not replace its compiler server with the macro client library.",
